{
  "_comment": "Character, end to end: Qwen-Image paints the concept and Hunyuan3D 2.1 ShapeGen turns it into a mesh, in one queue. Both are saved -- the picture as well as the mesh -- because a good concept is worth keeping even when the mesh it produced is not. Convenient but committing: the mesh is generated whether or not the concept was worth it, and a bad concept is the usual reason a mesh comes out as twenty disconnected pieces. The staged path (txt2img_qwen_fast to find the picture, then img2mesh_hunyuan3d21 on the one you like) wastes less. Hunyuan3D's licence excludes the EU, the UK and South Korea -- see README.md.",
